Dongala is a regency that spans about 300 km (180 m) north-west of the island of Sulawesi.
This regency with a lower status compared to the state has an approximate population of 299,20,200.
Fishing and farming are the main sources of the economy in Central Sulawesi, especially in the coastal areas of Dongala.
Nickel mines are also important in the state, but most of them are on the opposite side of the Sulawesi coast.
According to the Indonesian Disaster Response Agency, Palu and Dongala have been hit by many tsunamis in the past 100 years.
